---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import { SOCIAL_LINKS } from '../consts';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Software engineer passionate about building tools and exploring AI-assisted development"
	pubDate={new Date('January 01 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		Hi, I'm Justin Valentini, a software engineer based in New Hampshire. I've been writing code 
		since 2008 and have a passion for building tools that make developers' lives easier.
	</p>

	<h2>What I Do</h2>
	<p>
		I'm particularly interested in AI-assisted development and modern web technologies. I build 
		CLI tools, web applications, and automation solutions that help developers work more efficiently. 
		My recent projects include <a href="https://github.com/jvalentini/worklog" target="_blank">worklog</a>, 
		a tool for aggregating development activity from AI coding sessions, git commits, and GitHub activity.
	</p>

	<h2>Technology Stack</h2>
	<p>
		I work with a variety of technologies, with a current focus on:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Languages:</strong> TypeScript, JavaScript, Ruby, Python</li>
		<li><strong>Runtimes & Frameworks:</strong> Bun, Node.js, Astro, Rails</li>
		<li><strong>Tools & Practices:</strong> Biome, Oxlint, Git, AI coding assistants (Claude, Cursor)</li>
		<li><strong>Cloud & Infrastructure:</strong> Cloudflare Pages, Docker</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Development Philosophy</h2>
	<p>
		I believe in fast feedback loops, strict type safety, and leveraging modern tooling to move quickly 
		without sacrificing quality. AI coding assistants are powerful, but only when paired with robust 
		linting, formatting, and type checking to catch issues immediately.
	</p>

	<h2>Projects & Open Source</h2>
	<p>
		You can find my open source work on <a href={SOCIAL_LINKS.github} target="_blank">GitHub</a>, 
		where I maintain various projects ranging from CLI tools to web applications. I'm particularly 
		proud of recent work around developer productivity tooling.
	</p>

	<h2>Get in Touch</h2>
	<p>
		I'm always interested in connecting with other developers. You can reach me:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>LinkedIn: <a href={SOCIAL_LINKS.linkedin} target="_blank">linkedin.com/in/justinvalentini</a></li>
		<li>GitHub: <a href={SOCIAL_LINKS.github} target="_blank">github.com/jvalentini</a></li>
		<li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${SOCIAL_LINKS.email}`}>{SOCIAL_LINKS.email}</a></li>
	</ul>

	<p>
		Thanks for stopping by! Feel free to browse my <a href="/blog">blog posts</a> where I write 
		about software engineering, development workflows, and lessons learned from building projects.
	</p>
</Layout>
